CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-16
#   HIGH caddy: golang.org/x/net/html v0.60.0 — NOT REACHABLE: a denial of service in the HTML parser; Caddy parses HTML only in its templates module, and no Caddyfile (infra/edge, infra/lan, infra/onprem, infra/monitor, the api's log-filter.caddy) uses templates; no Caddy release carries x/net 0.62.0 yet (2.11.9-alpine rebuilt 2026-11-13, read 2026-11-16)

CVE-2026-97054 exp:2026-12-16
#   HIGH caddy, centrifugo, gotenberg, database (gosu): Go net/http (GO-2026-6859, fixed in Go 1.27.4 and 1.26.11) — NOT REACHABLE: the race needs a handler that wraps the request body in MaxBytesReader or MaxBytesHandler and reads it while writing the response header. Caddy: no Caddyfile sets request_body (infra/edge, infra/lan, infra/onprem, infra/monitor). Centrifugo: only `= /connection/websocket` is passed on (infra/web/nginx.conf), an upgrade with no body; its HTTP API is internal and key-held. Gotenberg publishes no port and hears only the api. gosu opens no server. The api's FrankenPHP 1.13.6 is built on go1.27.4, so it no longer carries it. No fixed release of caddy:2.11.9-alpine (digest unchanged 2026-11-20) or centrifugo (v6.10.3, 2026-11-08) exists yet; gotenberg 9.9.0 (2026-11-19) is a five-minor update with its own row (S5.67). Re-read 2026-11-20.

# The monitor machine (infra/monitor/compose.yaml), scanned since 2026-11-20: Gatus v5.38.0 and GlitchTip 7.0.0, neither with a
# newer release that day. Each verdict was read in the image itself (who imports the package, what serves HTTP, which
# binaries call the flawed path) against the monitor's configuration.

CVE-2026-116587 exp:2026-12-16
#   HIGH gatus (the monitor): go-jose v4.1.4 — NOT REACHABLE: a crafted RSA JWK; Gatus parses JWKs only for its OIDC sign-in, which infra/monitor/gatus.yaml does not configure (no security: block)

CVE-2026-63209 exp:2026-12-16
#   HIGH gatus (the monitor): klauspost/compress v1.18.6 — NOT REACHABLE: the overflow is in s2.NewDict on a dictionary the caller supplies; Gatus builds no s2 dictionary from anything it reads

CVE-2026-46603 exp:2026-12-16
#   HIGH gatus (the monitor): golang.org/x/image v0.40.0 — NOT REACHABLE: a crafted WebP (VP8L) image; Gatus decodes no image it is sent, its badges are written SVG

CVE-2026-116304 exp:2026-12-16
#   HIGH glitchtip (the monitor): libpq5 17.11 — NOT REACHABLE: PostgreSQL's 2026-11-12 fixes are in the server, its PL languages and the client tools (pg_dump, pg_restore, reindexdb), none of which libpq5 holds; its one libpq item (sslkeylogfile) needs the connection string, which the compose file fixes. The monitor's own glitchtip-db server takes 18.7 with the postgres bump (audit 2026-11-19 row 35)

